WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:22.012
At the sound of the maid's scream, Kathleen ran into Gerald's room.

2
00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:23.785
"What's wrong?"

3
00:00:23.786 --> 00:00:27.701
"One minute Gerald was gone!" said Eliza.

4
00:00:27.702 --> 00:00:30.468
"The next minute he was in the bed!

5
00:00:30.469 --> 00:00:32.754
I don't know what's wrong with me.

6
00:00:32.755 --> 00:00:37.137
Yesterday I was hearing voices, and now this."

7
00:00:37.138 --> 00:00:43.630
Eliza shook her head as she left the room.

8
00:00:43.631 --> 00:00:48.005
"What happened?" Kathleen asked Gerald.

9
00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:51.037
"The ring came off when Eliza called me.

10
00:00:51.038 --> 00:00:56.434
I'm hungry. I'll tell you everything later."

11
00:00:56.435 --> 00:01:02.048
After breakfast Gerald remembered he'd left the ring in bed.

12
00:01:02.049 --> 00:01:07.394
But when he went upstairs, Eliza had already made his bed.

13
00:01:07.395 --> 00:01:10.516
He asked her about the ring.

14
00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:13.488
"I didn't see anything," she said.

15
00:01:13.489 --> 00:01:19.211
"If there was a ring in the bed, I'd have seen it."

16
00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:25.748
The children searched every corner of the room, but couldn't find the ring.

17
00:01:25.749 --> 00:01:32.218
Soon they gave up because they had to meet Mabel in town.

18
00:01:32.219 --> 00:01:35.090
They sat on a wall to wait for her.

19
00:01:35.091 --> 00:01:44.214
"Hey, you went back to normal faster than I did," Mabel said to Gerald.

20
00:01:44.215 --> 00:01:49.705
Now Gerald could tell the story of the three burglars.

21
00:01:49.706 --> 00:01:57.470
After throwing the rock, he'd returned to the room where they were loading their sacks.

22
00:01:57.471 --> 00:02:04.681
He'd followed the men out into the night and discovered their hiding place.

23
00:02:04.682 --> 00:02:08.527
"Look, there's Officer Johnson," said Gerald.

24
00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:12.920
"I need to talk to him."

25
00:02:12.921 --> 00:02:18.751
Gerald hopped off the wall and went over to Officer Johnson.

26
00:02:18.752 --> 00:02:24.187
"Would you like to catch those burglars who've been stealing silver?"

27
00:02:24.188 --> 00:02:28.053
"What do you know about that?" Johnson asked suspiciously.

28
00:02:28.054 --> 00:02:32.361
"I saw something last night, but I could get in trouble for being out late.

29
00:02:32.362 --> 00:02:34.432
Do you promise not to tell anyone?"

30
00:02:34.433 --> 00:02:36.671
Johnson nodded.

31
00:02:36.672 --> 00:02:39.579
"I saw three men taking silver from the castle.

32
00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.551
I know where they put it."

33
00:02:41.552 --> 00:02:45.725
"So you wrote the note?" Johnson said eagerly.

34
00:02:45.726 --> 00:02:52.634
"Yes." Gerald explained how he'd watched the men go down to the river.

35
00:02:52.635 --> 00:02:56.874
They had tied their bags of silver under a dock.

36
00:02:56.875 --> 00:03:02.419
Tonight, after dark, they planned to retrieve the silver and escape by boat.

37
00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:05.874
"You can catch them then," said Gerald.

38
00:03:05.875 --> 00:03:10.651
"But which dock is their hiding spot?" asked Johnson.

39
00:03:10.652 --> 00:03:15.616
"Follow me," said Gerald.

40
00:03:15.617 --> 00:03:20.523
"When I take out my handkerchief and blow my nose, that'll be the place."

41
00:03:20.524 --> 00:03:24.930
Gerald went back to the other children.

42
00:03:24.931 --> 00:03:29.993
"Come on! Let's play follow-the-leader."

43
00:03:29.994 --> 00:03:35.469
The children followed him, running and jumping and imitating his every step.

44
00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:41.443
Johnson followed at a distance.

45
00:03:41.444 --> 00:03:46.194
On one dock Gerald suddenly stopped and blew his nose.

46
00:03:46.195 --> 00:03:55.840
Then he led the children back to the school.

47
00:03:55.841 --> 00:03:58.783
"We've brought our friend Mabel home for lunch,"

48
00:03:58.784 --> 00:04:01.889
said Kathleen when Eliza opened the door.

49
00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.314
"Where's Mademoiselle?"

50
00:04:04.315 --> 00:04:06.344
"She's gone to visit the castle.

51
00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.744
The grounds are open to the public today.

52
00:04:08.745 --> 00:04:10.563
Now hurry up with your lunch.

53
00:04:10.564 --> 00:04:12.523
This is my afternoon off.

54
00:04:12.524 --> 00:04:21.124
My fiancé doesn't like waiting for me."

55
00:04:21.125 --> 00:04:24.277
The children ate quickly and Eliza left.

56
00:04:24.278 --> 00:04:27.824
"Where's the ring?" asked Mabel.

57
00:04:27.825 --> 00:04:30.390
"I really need to put it back."

58
00:04:30.391 --> 00:04:33.952
"I haven't had a turn yet," protested Jimmy.

59
00:04:33.953 --> 00:04:36.683
"When we find it—"

60
00:04:36.684 --> 00:04:40.079
"When you find it?" said Mabel.

61
00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:44.703
They told her about losing the ring.

62
00:04:44.704 --> 00:04:47.739
"Oh no!" cried Mabel.

63
00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:50.965
"We have to find it!"

64
00:04:50.966 --> 00:04:56.709
The children searched and searched Gerald's room, but they still couldn't find the ring.

65
00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:01.141
Suddenly there was pounding at the back door.

66
00:05:01.142 --> 00:05:03.522
Kathleen ran downstairs.

67
00:05:03.523 --> 00:05:08.618
A strange man stood near the doorstep.

68
00:05:08.619 --> 00:05:12.044
His eyes were open wide with amazement.

69
00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:15.015
One arm was stretched out toward the door.

70
00:05:15.016 --> 00:05:19.571
The rest of him looked as if he were trying to run the other way.

71
00:05:19.572 --> 00:05:22.370
"Let go of me!" he cried.

72
00:05:22.371 --> 00:05:26.362
"I won't let go of you!" said Eliza's voice.

73
00:05:26.363 --> 00:05:32.358
But no Eliza could be seen.
